  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "great_barrow",
      "name": "The Great Barrow",
      "class": "tomb",
      "offset": [
        40.0,
        0.0,
        36.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        44.5,
        0.05,
        39.5
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "great_barrow.entry",
        "great_barrow.hall",
        "great_barrow.tomb"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The only section built to be looked at: dressed granite, spiral carving, a colonnade and a raised dais.",
        "The tomb chamber is declared open_to_sky. A combined insides map has one environment, so the shaft will not currently show sky."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "root_crypt",
      "name": "The Root Crypt",
      "class": "crypt",
      "offset": [
        135.0,
        0.0,
        36.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        138.0,
        0.05,
        38.75
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "root_crypt.stairhead",
        "root_crypt.rootfall",
        "root_crypt.underchamber"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "The counterweight to the Great Barrow: no dressed stone, earth floors, and the roots of the moor's dead trees through the roof.",
        "Root geometry comes from the toolkit's own `root_ribs`, which is what it was written for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bone_gallery",
      "name": "The Bone Gallery",
      "class": "ossuary",
      "offset": [
        40.0,
        0.0,
        141.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        43.0,
        0.05,
        143.5
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "bone_gallery.stairhead",
        "bone_gallery.gallery",
        "bone_gallery.altar",
        "bone_gallery.trapcell"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Dry, long and mean. The niches are what make it a gallery rather than a corridor with candles in it.",
        "The stake corridor is the only part of these barrows built to keep people out. It is walkable: the stakes are geometry, not collision, and the trap is the server's to run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fen_crypt",
      "name": "The Fen Crypt",
      "class": "flooded",
      "offset": [
        135.0,
        0.0,
        141.0
      ],
      "arrival": [
        138.0,
        0.05,
        143.5
      ],
      "spaces": [
        "fen_crypt.stairhead",
        "fen_crypt.ossuary"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Shin-deep standing water over the ossuary floor, with a drystone shelf and a causeway a step up out of it. The floor is waded rather than blocked, because the toolkit's chamber floor is always a walk surface and a drowned-but-walkable floor would have been a lie.",
        "Bog water here is the region's own opaque `grey_bog_water`, not a transparent lake: peat stain kills the light that enters it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fifth_chamber",
